# CeraLive: keep Quectel RM520N modems on USB 2 (AT+QCFG="usbspeed","20").
# Their own USB 3 link raises the receiver's noise floor; see the script's header.
# One oneshot instance per added USB device (coldplug included), keyed by its
# kernel name, e.g. ceralive-modem-usbspeed@5-1.4.service. The model check
# (RM520N only; the RM530N-GL shares this ID) and every decision are in the
# script. add-only: the module's own reset re-adds the device, which is how the
# result gets verified.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="2c7c", ATTR{idProduct}=="0801", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ceralive-modem-usbspeed@%k.service"
